1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,310
Caspion was a small silver fish who loved to swim faster and farther than all the others.

2
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:17,800
Caspion: Come on, everybody! Let's see what's beyond the reef!

3
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:25,080
But his friends were afraid to leave the reef, so Caspion set out alone.

4
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:29,750
Far from home, Caspion heard someone crying.

5
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:36,150
Caspion: Why are you crying, little whale?

6
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:41,930
Little Whale: I lost my mother in the storm... I'm all alone.

7
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:48,480
Caspion: Don't worry. I'll help you find her!

8
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:09,460
Shark: Well, well... a snack and a dessert.

9
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:14,690
Caspion: Help!

10
00:01:14,690 --> 00:01:18,260
Mother Whale: Leave those little ones alone!

11
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:27,260
Little Whale: Mama! You found me!

12
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:32,010
Little Whale: This is Caspion. He helped me!

13
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:36,200
Mother Whale: Thank you, brave little fish.

14
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:46,500
Octopus: So you want to see the world above the water, little fish?

15
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,450
Caspion: More than anything!

16
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:57,370
Octopus: Then my friend the jellyfish will carry you, with the sea held in her bell.

17
00:02:11,370 --> 00:02:19,620
And so Caspion rose up, up, up... until he saw the sky for the very first time.

18
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:34,250
Caspion: The world is simply wonderful... wet or dry!

19
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:37,250
העולם פשוט נפלא, רטוב או יבש!

